1. P1 — concurrent `check` runs can overwrite each other’s verdicts. Captures use the same SHA/role filenames, while the lock covers each attest phase separately and is released before transcripts are reread. A run whose reviewer returned `VERDICT: FAIL` with exit 0 can consume another concurrent run’s `PASS` transcript and emit `SAFE TO MERGE`. Use run-unique artifacts or hold the lock through capture, verdict parsing, and final evaluation. [bin/coverloop:981](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:981), [bin/coverloop:2728](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2728), [bin/coverloop:2768](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2768), [bin/coverloop:2770](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2770)

2. P1 — test-gate weakening is detected only when the `test_command` string changes. An unchanged command such as `./test.sh` can have its referenced script replaced with `exit 0`; that path remains L1, no reviewer is scheduled, and the no-op test earns `SAFE TO MERGE`. Test harness changes need an L2 floor or content binding to the reviewed command. [bin/coverloop:545](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:545), [bin/coverloop:2570](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2570), [bin/coverloop:2678](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2678)

